{
  "id": "ss.char.hex",
  "name": "Hex",
  "description": "The one with a lot of small things to look after. Orchid hair in a bob with a six-sided clip in it, brows up and in, a small wavering mouth, and on the back, carried like a pack on a strap, a brood vent: the puckered plate that pushes out grubs. Two grubs ride it already, one over the shoulder and one at the hip, and they never stop moving, because a grub does not know it is not at home. The dress is tiled with the hive's cells — the hexagon it used to be. The arms are the slightest on the roster; Hex does not hit anything itself, it sends things. Same dead organ as the rest, worn as a brooch; same bobble feelers. Drawn facing +x; the game flips it.",
